  <text>
    <body>
      <p>A fox challenged a stone to a race; this one excused itself:</p>
      <p>"I'm very heavy."</p>
      <p>"We will run down that hill," the fox insisted.</p>
      <p>"I am very heavy ... but beware of me ..."</p>
      <p>"You will catch up with me? What madness! I run like the wind."</p>
      <p>"Alright, let's run," said the stone.</p>
      <p>And the fox left like an arrow ... The stone then began to roll, and from tumble to tumble, he went to mortally wound its rival, who had already reached the foot of the hill.</p>
    </body>
